## Building a Mini App Suite

### Menu System

```xiom
fn show_menu() {
  io.println("=== Mini App Suite ===");
  io.println("1. Calculator");
  io.println("2. Tip Calculator");
  io.println("3. Number Guessing Game");
  io.println("4. To-Do List");
  io.println("5. Countdown Timer");
  io.println("0. Exit");
}

fn run_app(choice: Int) {
  if choice == 1 { run_calculator(); }
  else if choice == 2 { run_tip_calculator(); }
  else if choice == 3 { run_guessing_game(); }
  else if choice == 4 { run_todo_list(); }
  else if choice == 5 { run_timer(); }
}
```

### Main Loop

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let mut running = true;
  while running {
    show_menu();
    let choice = 1;

    if choice == 0 {
      running = false;
      io.println("Goodbye!");
    } else {
      run_app(choice);
    };
  };
  return 0;
}
```

### Integrating Components

Each tool is a function that runs independently and returns to the menu:

```xiom
fn run_calculator() {
  io.println("Calculator: 5 + 3 = 8");
}

fn run_tip_calculator() {
  io.println("Tip: $100 at 18% = $18 tip");
}

fn run_guessing_game() {
  io.println("Guess the number! (42)");
}

fn run_todo_list() {
  io.println("TODO: 3 items pending");
}

fn run_timer() {
  io.println("Timer: 5...4...3...2...1...Done!");
}
```

### Architecture Pattern

```
Menu
 ├── Calculator (add/sub/mul/div)
 ├── Tip Calculator (bill, %, split)
 ├── Guessing Game (random, hints)
 ├── To-Do List (add/complete/remove)
 └── Timer (countdown, format)
```

### Why This Matters

Real software is composed of multiple features. The menu pattern is used in ATMs, POS systems, game main menus, and developer CLIs. Mastering it means you can build ANY multi-feature application.

